* Model of a electric arc
* The model has its roots in the classical Cassie and Mayr
* equations, which were used extensively in the past to explain the
* physics of arc plasma operation. The equations of the proposed
* model have been cast in a form suitable for implementation in
* industrial-standard circuit simulators.

* each half-cycle (10ms) of the AC supply voltage, the arc is
* momentarily extinguished and then re-ignited

*  From:
*  Dynamic electric arc model for electronic circuit simulation
*  Article in Electronics Letters · May 1996
*
*  see electric arc electric_arc_modelling.pdf in this folder
*  (For the example in the pdf the value of gmin is changed from 1e-8 to 0.15e-3 to work correctly
*   for the parameters p0 and e0 in this pdf)
*
* E0 = 28,
* Io = 4.8,
* Po = 30,
* Gmin= 1*1e-8 (0.15e-3)
* Theta=1e-4
* Cassie Mayr:
* G=Gmin+(1-exp(-i*i/(I0*I0))) *v*i/(E0*E0) +(exp(-i*i/(I0*I0)))*i*i/P0 -Theta*dG/dt
* i=G.v
* a1=(1-exp(-i*i/(I0*I0))) *v*i/(E0*E0)  v=v(in1,out) i=I(V0) oder I(G0)
* b1=(exp(-i*i/(I0*I0)))*i*i/P0
* FOR:
* i0 very small: e-10000 = sehr klein a1=1 b1=0 hoher strom eher cassie model
* i0 very high:  e-0.001 = 1  a1=0 b1=1 kleiner strom eher mayr model


* cassie / mayr model
*(1-exp(-i*i/(I0*I0)))*v*i/(E0*E0) cassie
*(exp(-i*i/(I0*I0)))*i*i/P0   mayr 
.subckt arc in out params: e0=0.0028 i0=6 p0=0.02 gmin=1e-7 theta=1e-4 ginit=0
V0 in in1 0
E1 a1 0 VALUE={(1-exp(-(i(v0)*i(v0))/(I0*I0)))*((v(in1,out)*i(v0))/(E0*E0))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
E2 b1 0 VALUE={(exp(-(i(v0)*i(v0))/(I0*I0)))*((i(v0)*i(v0))/P0)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
EG G 0 VALUE={v(idt1)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
G1x 0 idt1  VALUE={(-v(G)+Gmin+v(a1)+v(b1))/Theta} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
C1x idt1 0 1 IC={ginit}
R1x idt1 0 1e10
G0 in1 out value={V(in1,out)*v(G)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
.ends

* only mayr model (good for smaller currents)
.subckt arc_mayr in out params: p0=0.06 gmin=1e-7 theta=1e-4 ginit=0
V0 in in1 0
E2 b1 0 VALUE={((i(v0)*i(v0))/P0)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
EG G 0 VALUE={v(idt1)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
G1x 0 idt1  VALUE={(-v(G)+Gmin+v(b1))/Theta} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
C1x idt1 0 1 IC={ginit}
R1x idt1 0 1e10
G0 in1 out value={V(in1,out)*v(G)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
.ends

* only cassie model (good for higher currents)
.subckt arc_cassie in out params: e0=0.0028 gmin=1e-7 theta=1e-4 ginit=0
V0 in in1 0
E1 a1 0 VALUE={((v(in1,out)*i(v0))/(E0*E0))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
EG G 0 VALUE={v(idt1)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
G1x 0 idt1  VALUE={(-v(G)+Gmin+v(a1))/Theta} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
C1x idt1 0 1 IC={ginit}
R1x idt1 0 1e10
G0 in1 out value={V(in1,out)*v(G)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
.ends

* only mayr model with controlling nodes (good for smaller currents)
.subckt arc_mayr_ctrl in out P0 E0 Theta Gmin params: p0=0.06 gmin=1e-7 theta=1e-4 ginit=0
V0 in in1 0
E2 b1 0 VALUE={((i(v0)*i(v0))/(P0*v(P0)))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
EG G 0 VALUE={v(idt1)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
G1x 0 idt1  VALUE={(-v(G)+Gmin*v(Gmin)+v(b1))/(Theta*v(Theta))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
C1x idt1 0 1 IC={ginit}
R1x idt1 0 1e10
G0 in1 out value={V(in1,out)*v(G)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
.ends

* only mayr model with controlling nodes (good for smaller currents)
.subckt arc_cassie_ctrl in out P0 E0 Theta Gmin 
+ params: e0=100 gmin=1e-7 theta=1e-4 ginit=0
V0 in in1 0
E1 a1 0 VALUE={((v(in1,out)*i(v0))/(e0*e0)*v(e0)*v(e0))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
EG G 0 VALUE={v(idt1)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
G1x 0 idt1  VALUE={(-v(G)+Gmin*v(Gmin)+v(a1))/(Theta*v(Theta))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
C1x idt1 0 1 IC={ginit}
R1x idt1 0 1e10
G0 in1 out value={V(in1,out)*v(G)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
.ends

* cassie / mayr model with controlling nodes
.subckt arc_ctrl in out P0 E0 Theta Gmin params: e0=0.0028 i0=6 p0=0.02 gmin=1e-7 theta=1e-4 ginit=0
V0 in in1 0
E1 a1 0 VALUE={(1-exp(-(i(v0)*i(v0))/(I0*I0)))*((v(in1,out)*i(v0))/(E0*E0*v(e0)*v(e0)))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
E2 b1 0 VALUE={(exp(-(i(v0)*i(v0))/(I0*I0)))*((i(v0)*i(v0))/(P0*v(p0)*v(p0)))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
EG G 0 VALUE={v(idt1)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
G1x 0 idt1  VALUE={(-v(G)+Gmin*v(Gmin)+v(a1)+v(b1))/(Theta*v(Theta))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
C1x idt1 0 1 IC={ginit}
R1x idt1 0 1e10
G0 in1 out value={V(in1,out)*v(G)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
.ends


* Behavioural simple fuse model
* If I>Imin_melt the current is integrated
* until i2tmax is reached now the
* fuse melts.
* Means that i2tmax is very small
* the melting is immdiately
* If i2tmax is very high
* the fuse can melt later and at higher currents
.subckt fuse in out params: rfuse=0.5 i2tmax=0.07 Imin_melt=0.5 tsw=100m vt=0.5 vh=-0.4
vIsense in in1 0
rfuse in1 in2 {rfuse}
s1 in2 out ctrl 0 myswitch
bctrl ctrl1 0 v={if(v(i2t)>i2tmax,1,0)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
Ectrl2 ctrl 0 value={v(idt1)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
G1x 0 idt1  VALUE={(v(ctrl1)/tsw)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
C1x idt1 0 1 IC=0
R1x idt1 0 1e10
bcond conditioned 0 v={if(abs(i(vIsense))>Imin_melt,abs(I(vIsense)),0)}   tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
bi2t i2t 0 v=v(idt2) tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
G2x 0 idt2 VALUE={v(conditioned)**2} tripdv=1 tripdt=1
C2x idt2 0 1
R2x idt2 0 1e10
.model myswitch SW ( ron=1e9 roff=0.01 vt={vt} vh={vh} )
.ends


.subckt ameter1 vin vout I
+ params: fc=3 tdv=1 tdt=1 tenable=1u
Vamper vin vout 0
Eamper I1 0 VALUE={IF(time>tenable,I(Vamper),0)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
XU4 I1 I RMS3b fc={fc} b0=1 b1=3
.ends

.subckt RMS3b in out params: fc=3 b0=3 b1=3 lim=1g
Asq 0 in in 0 0 0 sq 0 ota vhigh={lim} rout=1 linear
Adiv_lf _sq sq 0 0 0 0 div 0 ota vhigh={lim} rout=1g cout={1n/fc} linear
Adiv 0 div out 0 0 0 _sq 0 ota vhigh={lim} rout=1 linear
Ab0 out div 0 0 0 0 1 0 ota vhigh={lim} vlow={-lim} cout={.5/pi/fc} rout=1g g={b0/b1} linear
Ab1 out 1 0 0 0 0 out 0 ota vhigh={lim} vlow={-lim} cout={.5/pi/fc} rout=1g g={b1} linear
.ends RMS1


.subckt fuse_20A in out params: rfuse=0.01 i2tmax=0.07 Imin_melt=20 tsw=100m vt=0.5 vh=-0.4
vIsense in in1 0
rfuse in1 in2 {rfuse}
s1 in2 out ctrl 0 myswitch
bctrl ctrl1 0 v={if(v(i2t)>i2tmax,1,0)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
Ectrl2 ctrl 0 value={v(idt1)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
G1x 0 idt1  VALUE={(v(ctrl1)/tsw)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
C1x idt1 0 1 IC=0
R1x idt1 0 1e10
bcond conditioned 0 v={if(abs(i(vIsense))>Imin_melt,abs(I(vIsense)),0)}   tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
bi2t i2t 0 v=v(idt2) tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
G2x 0 idt2 VALUE={v(conditioned)**2} tripdv=1 tripdt=1
C2x idt2 0 1
R2x idt2 0 1e10
.model myswitch SW ( ron=1e9 roff=0.01 vt=0.5 vh=-0.4 )
.ends

